WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.323
Closing the elective.

2
00:00:01.603 --> 00:00:05.891
You started this elective relying on an agent without knowing what was best.

3
00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:24.091
You now have the parts: how the loop and context work, what benchmarks and studies do and don’t show, how to choose tools and settings with evidence, how to give context that changes behavior, how to make checks run by default, how to review and secure agent work, and when to keep the work yourself.

4
00:00:24.371 --> 00:00:29.448
The project asks you to put all of it on one of your own repositories and measure the difference.

5
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:38.325
The habit to keep afterwards is the one under all the others: treat every claim, including the agent’s “done,” as a hypothesis you can check.
